Disclosure: the site's author works at Wiz.
notes:
These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites, over two slides. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

Wiz's post is the source of the assessed ESRP root cause, the chart of the publish and the victim count; Wiz added the ESRP finding on November 18, and the Wayback Machine holds the original November 17 version. As the page discloses, the root-cause assessment and the victim count come from Wiz Research, and the site's author works at Wiz. Microsoft has not confirmed the assessment.

PyPI's advisory, PYSEC-2026-4388, is the registry's own account. JFrog read the repack and the payload, StepSecurity gives the timeline of quarantines and uploads, and SafeDep, Socket and Aikido published their own analyses.

== Primary sources, continued
layout: links
link: Chainguard, agent-framework compromised on PyPI | https://www.chainguard.dev/unchained/microsoft-agent-framework-compromised-on-pypi-november-2026
link: OpenSourceMalware, official agent-framework package compromised | https://opensourcemalware.com/blog/agent-framework-pypi-compromised
